questions.explanation:
Evaluate both expressions:
\[
\begin{aligned}
2^{-3} &= \frac{1}{2^3}=\frac{1}{8}\\
3^{-2} &= \frac{1}{3^2}=\frac{1}{9}
\end{aligned}
\]
Since \(\frac{1}{8}>\frac{1}{9}\), we have \(2^{-3}>3^{-2}\). Therefore, \(2^{-3}\) is greater.

A negative exponent on a fraction inverts the fraction and makes the exponent positive:
\[
\begin{aligned}
\left(\frac{2}{3}\right)^{-2} &= \left(\frac{3}{2}\right)^2\\
\left(\frac{3}{2}\right)^2 &= \frac{3^2}{2^2}=\frac{9}{4}
\end{aligned}
\]
The choice "\(\frac{4}{9}\)" incorrectly squares the original fraction without inverting it.
